    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Parse Google Trends responses and combine all context\nconst moroccoRaw = $('Fetch Trends: Morocco').first().json.data || '';\nconst stats = $('Fetch Udarsy Stats').first().json;\nconst latestContent = $('Fetch Udarsy Latest Content').first().json;\n\n// Parse trends (Google Trends returns JSONP-like format, strip prefix)\nlet moroccoTrends = [];\n\ntry {\n  const moroccoJson = JSON.parse(moroccoRaw.replace(/^\\)\\]\\}\\'\\n/, ''));\n  moroccoTrends = moroccoJson.default?.trendingSearchesDays?.[0]?.trendingSearches?.map(t => t.title?.query) || [];\n} catch (e) {\n  moroccoTrends = ['education', 'bac 2026', 'university'];\n}\n\ntry {\n  const moroccoJson = JSON.parse(moroccoRaw.replace(/^\\)\\]\\}\\'\\n/, ''));\n  moroccoTrends = moroccoJson.default?.trendingSearchesDays?.[0]?.trendingSearches?.map(t => t.title?.query) || [];\n} catch (e) {\n  moroccoTrends = ['education', 'baccalaureat', 'universite'];\n}\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    morocco_trends: moroccoTrends.slice(0, 10),\n    udarsy_stats: stats,\n    latest_content: latestContent,\n    date: new Date().toISOString().split('T')[0]\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "id": "combine-context",
      "name": "Combine All Context",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        500,
        400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions",
        "authentication": "predefinedCredentialType",
        "nodeCredentialType": "openAiApi",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ model: \"gpt-4o\", messages: [{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"You are a viral marketing expert specializing in educational platforms in North Africa (Morocco). You understand Arabic social media culture, Moroccan dialect, and what makes educational content go viral among students aged 15-25.\\n\\nYour task: Generate 10 viral social media hook ideas for Udarsy (دارسي), a Moroccan educational platform targeting BAC and Brevet students. Currency: MAD. School calendar: BAC in June, Brevet in May, back to school in September.\\n\\nFor EACH hook, provide:\\n1. hook_ar: The hook in Arabic (Moroccan dialect)\\n2. hook_fr: The hook in French\\n3. hook_en: The hook in English\\n4. platform: Best platform (instagram/tiktok/facebook/twitter)\\n5. format: Content format (reel/carousel/story/post/thread)\\n6. virality_score: 1-10 prediction of viral potential\\n7. reasoning: Why this could go viral (in English)\\n8. cta: Call to action\\n9. hashtags: 5 relevant hashtags\\n10. tie_to_trend: Which trend this connects to (if any)\\n\\nRespond with a JSON array of 10 objects.\\n\\nGuidelines:\\n- Use relatable student humor and situations\\n- Reference exam seasons, study struggles, university life\\n- Leverage current trends from the provided data\\n- Mix educational value with entertainment\\n- Include hooks that work for Reels/TikTok (short-form video)\\n- Some hooks should promote Udarsy features directly\\n- Some should be pure value/entertainment that builds brand awareness\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"=Date: {{ $json.date }}\\n\\nTrending in Morocco: {{ $json.morocco_trends.join(', ') }}\\n\\nUdarsy stats: {{ JSON.stringify($json.udarsy_stats || {}) }}\\nLatest content: {{ JSON.stringify($json.latest_content?.data?.slice(0, 3) || []) }}\\n\\nGenerate 10 viral hook ideas!\"}], temperature: 0.9, max_tokens: 4000 }) }}",
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "responseFormat": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "ai-generate-hooks",
      "name": "GPT-4o: Generate 10 Hooks",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        740,
        400
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "openAiApi": {
          "id": "openai-api",
          "name": "OpenAI account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const item = $input.first().json;\nconst content = item.message?.content || item.choices?.[0]?.message?.content || '[]';\n\nlet hooks;\ntry {\n  // Handle potential markdown code fences\n  const cleaned = content.replace(/```json\\n?/g, '').replace(/```\\n?/g, '').trim();\n  hooks = JSON.parse(cleaned);\n} catch (e) {\n  hooks = [{ hook_ar: 'Parse error', hook_fr: 'Parse error', hook_en: content, virality_score: 0 }];\n}\n\n// Sort by virality score descending\nhooks.sort((a, b) => (b.virality_score || 0) - (a.virality_score || 0));\n\n// Return each hook as a separate item\nreturn hooks.map((hook, i) => ({\n  json: {\n    ...hook,\n    rank: i + 1\n  }\n}));"
      },
      "id": "parse-and-score-hooks",
      "name": "Parse & Score Hooks",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
